It doesn't need to be a free square. The statement you quoted was
saying that you should filter additional boulders remains from the
players square. The rationale for that was, as per the suggestion,
that objects on the player's square will be re-linked from the
disrupted level into a new version of that level that will become
the bones level. The prominent obvious item that might be a problem
in Sokoban would be a boulder. So filtering boulders on the player's
square could in a simple way avoid any potential problems with such
spare boulders. (N.B.: You would have to filter the object chain
_before_ you link the objects to the new level, otherwise you could
remove one of the initial boulders if the player dies on any such
spot.) It may even be an option to omit that boulder filtering and
keep even a boulder on the players square - who cares! (The latter
case could, in Sokoban, only happen if the player squeezes onto the
boulder square, got there polymorphed, or if he read a (cursed or
uncursed) scroll of earth on that spot, or if he fell from above
onto a square with a boulder. So it could be comparably simple -
and mind, comparably simple does not mean that you get it for free
- if one really intends to extend the bones mechanism to Sokoban.
YMMV.

